@flexiarg operator/port-via-breadcrumbs
@title Port Via Breadcrumbs
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 9 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-B4uQ4S turn-GxkKom turn-KrdAAA turn-Sh1Sfq turn-YnE8TC turn-heMCxh turn-hvAlC5 turn-oCTsYq turn-t4Q4wl; first proposed for: An implementation exists in one language (possibly partial) and the operator wants it in another language, and could either hand over a fresh spec or reuse the existing code.
@why [peeragogy/use-or-make]

! conclusion: Treat the existing partial implementation as breadcrumbs and as a guide to a sensible implementation order for the port, rather than starting from a blank plan.

  + IF:
    A prior partial implementation in the source language is available.

  + HOWEVER:
    Reusing the prior attempt risks importing its mistakes, but ignoring it wastes the ordering and design knowledge already paid for.

  + THEN:
    Treat the existing partial implementation as breadcrumbs and as a guide to a sensible implementation order for the port, rather than starting from a blank plan.

  + BECAUSE:
    It specialises use-or-make to the porting case: the reuse decision is made deliberately, and the reused artifact's specific role is sequencing the new implementation.
